From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakob Linke <jgruber@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 13:38:13 +0200
Subject: [turbolev] Fix expression invalidation at loop headers

MergeForLoop compares effect epochs from graph building and KNA
recomputation. These counters belong to different traversals, so equal
values can incorrectly preserve stale loads across loop effects.

Save the loop header's builder epoch and compare it with the saved
backedge epoch. During recomputation, invalidate epoch-dependent
expressions when that comparison indicates effects; otherwise retain
valid forward expressions. Treat epoch overflow conservatively.

This replaces backedge expression matching with loop-effect filtering.
Add a regression test and unit coverage for both backedge paths,
effectless loops, and stale forward expressions.

Fixed: 567175125
Change-Id: I3bf29885c7c7bd8c67475d1305c2fa8844cfdbed
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8493491
Reviewed-by: Darius Mercadier <dmercadier@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Jakob Linke <jgruber@chromium.org>
Auto-Submit: Jakob Linke <jgruber@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#110355}

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y): V8 15.2 has no
LoopMergePointInterpreterFrameState subclass; loop-header state lives
directly on MergePointInterpreterFrameState. InitializeLoopEffectEpoch(),
loop_has_effects() and loop_header_effect_epoch_ are therefore added to
MergePointInterpreterFrameState (next to backedge_known_node_aspects_),
InitializeLoop() calls InitializeLoopEffectEpoch() directly, and
RecomputeKnownNodeAspectsProcessor passes block->state()->loop_has_effects().
The V8_EXPORT_PRIVATE additions that only serve the new unittest are kept
where the declarations exist; MayBeHoleOrUndefinedNan() does not exist
here and the new unittest file changes are dropped (test-only).

